Z||000007||theogre||10-10-2000||09:11 AM||||webtv... get a real computer.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I didn't figure those would work.<P>Actually it will work for users with cable or DSL. There's just not whole lot of need unless your cable goes out allot.<P>It makes life handy with modems. pages load instantly.<P>Also handy if you are behind a firewall/proxy. you can open the channel all you want offline and some git won't see you in the logs but once. (Won't see you at all if you have a modem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>I've got it configured so it's not to disk space hungry. It takes less the 600K of disk space right now. takes only a couple minutes to load the whole mess via modem.<P>The Icon was tough. It took awhile to get it to look decent. Hard to fit a car in that small a parking space. And you all thought parallel parking was a ______.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-10-2000).]||||reg||10
