Z||000009||theogre||10-12-2000||09:23 AM||||Hmmmmm can't think of anything that should cause that. I have IE5.5 it works perfectly with it. Tried it at work and the channel synced up as soon as I clicked OK, which is just what it should normally do. Took about 2-3 minutes via modem.<P>There's nothing in the package that downloads but text and pictures.<P>I noticed the connections to europe where running real slow last night. That could cause it to look hung. Syncro is handled by a plugin. It should have opened a window or put an Icon in the system tray when it started.<P>IE and Win9x will do queer things after running for days. Maybe you just need a reboot?||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||10-23-2000||10:36 PM||||It's official! The Internet Explorer Channel feature is now part of Tunnel #6, The Fiero Cave.<P>You can now view the service related content of Tunnel #6 offline. Handy for modem users. Lapptop owners can now take the cave to your car while you work.<P>I've left some pages out of the channel's offline storage to conserve disk space. All pages work if you are connected. (So far that means I left our about 4 pages.)<P><A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/ogre.cdf" TARGET=_blank>Click Me to subscribe.</A><P>The main entrance to the cave <A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre" TARGET=_blank>is here.</A> This entrance works for all browsers, but only online.<BR>||||reg||1
